 "performing_artist_analysis": "<p>&quot;Front Door Famous&quot; opens Luke Combs&#39; fifth studio album, <em>Fathers &amp; Sons</em>, which debuted at No. 6 on the Billboard 200 in June 2024. Combs is one of the defining artists of modern country: a Grand Ole Opry member with a long run of No. 1 country-radio singles and a diamond-certified hit in &quot;Beautiful Crazy,&quot; and a repeat CMA, ACM, and Billboard Music Award winner.<br /><br />&quot;I Hate Alabama&quot; was Conner Smith&#39;s debut single and his breakout. It went viral on TikTok and reached No. 21 on Billboard&#39;s Country Digital Song Sales chart in late 2021, surging when Georgia beat Alabama for the national championship that January &mdash; success that earned Smith his Big Machine/Valory deal and Billboard&#39;s Country Rookie of the Month. He has since reached the Hot 100 and topped the UK Country Airplay chart with &quot;Creek Will Rise.&quot;<br /><br />&quot;Get Up and Get It&quot; comes from Drew Green, a Sony Music Nashville singer-songwriter who first broke in as a writer. &quot;Throwin&#39; Parties&quot; is the catalog&#39;s longest-tenured song and its most telling credit. It&#39;s recorded by Hunter Phelps, one of Nashville&#39;s premier hit songwriters &mdash; a Warner Chappell/Tape Room writer behind a string of No. 1 country singles including HARDY and Lainey Wilson&#39;s &quot;wait in the truck,&quot; HARDY&#39;s &quot;TRUCK BED,&quot; and Chris Lane&#39;s &quot;I Don&#39;t Know About You,&quot; plus a CMA Triple Play Award. Phelps also co-wrote two other songs in this catalog, a reminder that these cuts come from the same tight circle of Nashville writers.</p>",
