 "valuation_description": {
  "id": 7250,
  "contents": [
   {
    "id": 27424,
    "body": "<p>This catalog is built from a run of major-artist country cuts &mdash; five songs by five charting artists: Luke Combs, Conner Smith, Drew Green, Jon Langston, and Hunter Phelps. The anchor, &quot;Front Door Famous,&quot; recorded by Luke Combs on his 2024 album Fathers &amp; Sons, roughly doubled its writing income from the first year to the second.&nbsp;<br /><br />most modern country, it earns primarily through streaming, about 90% of income. What sets it apart is the balance. That streaming is spread evenly across platforms rather than riding on one. Apple Music, Spotify, and Pandora each take roughly a fifth to a quarter, with YouTube and Amazon behind them. No single service carries the catalog.<br /><br />last twelve months earned about $2,899 &mdash; within 2% of the three-year average of $2,838, and slightly above it. Even though the trailing year is down about 16% from the one before, that prior year was a peak lifted by the Combs cut&#39;s first-year streaming burst; the pullback simply returns earnings to their baseline.<br /><br />an investor, this is a focused bet on recent, streaming-era country songwriting: broad platform income from multiple charting artists, already settled at its floor rather than still cooling from a spike.</p>",
    "kind": "overview"
   },
   {
    "id": 27425,
    "body": "<p>Front Door Famous &mdash; 2024<br />catalog&#39;s largest earner at roughly 40% of recent income, recorded by Luke Combs, with writing royalties that roughly doubled from its first full year to its second.<br /><br />Up and Get It &mdash; 2021<br />31% of recent income and one of the steadiest quarter-to-quarter earners in the catalog, recorded by Drew Green.<br /><br />Hate Alabama &mdash; 2021<br />20% of recent income, recorded by Conner Smith, and the one top track that posted its strongest quarter in the most recent period and has maintained a positive CAGR of 7.92%.</p>",
    "kind": "song_analysis"
   },
   {
    "id": 27426,
    "body": "",
    "kind": "income_type_analysis"
   },
   {
    "id": 27427,
    "body": "<p>Streaming has been the dominant revenue source, contributing between 88.01% and 95.32% of total earnings annually.</p>",
    "kind": "source_analysis"
   },
   {
    "id": 27428,
    "body": "<p>Apple Music (about 24% of LTM)<br />single largest platform, reflecting Apple&#39;s higher per-play performance rates and no free tier.<br /><br />(about 23% of LTM)<br />level with Apple and the largest by raw listenership, a core and stable channel.<br /><br />(about 20% of LTM)<br />unusually prominent share, a good sign for country writing income given Pandora&#39;s radio-style listening and its strength with U.S. country audiences.<br />&nbsp;</p>",
    "kind": "music_user_analysis"
   },
   {
    "id": 27429,
    "body": "",
    "kind": "performing_artist_analysis"
   }
